  "query_preview": "..\n\nFog and low stratus currently present over western portions of \nNorth Dakota will spread into Daniels, Sheridan, and Roosevelt \ncounties through early this morning before clearing by early\nafternoon at the latest. While overall visibilities are not \nanticipated to be as reduced as they were yesterday morning, \nlocalized regions may see values as low as 1/4 mile between 09Z \nand 16Z.\n\nWidespread Chinook arch clouds are obstructing surface \nsatellite imagery, inhibiting the ability to monitor fog \nprogression at this time.\n\nAn upper-level ridge over Montana will result in dry conditions \nand temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above seasonal averages \npersisting through Tuesday.\n\nAn upper-level trough will dig over Montana by Wednesday,\nresulting in southwest flow aloft and subsequent cooler and \npotentially wetter weather.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Confidence in fog placement and visibilities this morning is\n  moderate (70%).\n \n- Confidence in fair conditions persisting through Monday is high\n  (90%). Confidence in fair conditions persisting through Tuesday\n  is moderate (70%).\n\n- Confidence in mid-week trough timing is on the low end of\n  moderate (40%).\n\n\nDON",
